1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:06,574
This is Bond, a non-custodial escrow for USDC, printed directly on Base.

2
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:11,370
Paying for work online still runs on trust.

3
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:17,526
Invoices disappear, deposits vanish, and nobody prints the proof of who owes what.

4
00:00:18,626 --> 00:00:22,154
Bond replaces that trust with a contract.

5
00:00:22,334 --> 00:00:27,614
The payee writes the terms into a link: amount, deadline, and arbiter.

6
00:00:27,794 --> 00:00:32,498
The payer reviews it, signs, and the contract locks the funds.

7
00:00:33,598 --> 00:00:38,278
The work is delivered, and on confirmation, the money releases.

8
00:00:38,458 --> 00:00:43,546
Disputes go to a single arbiter, and every deadline opens a way out.

9
00:00:44,646 --> 00:00:49,542
Inside the paper: milestone escrows that settle slice by slice.

10
00:00:49,722 --> 00:00:53,898
Payment requests that travel as a link and a QR code.

11
00:00:54,078 --> 00:00:58,062
A reputation dossier read straight from the ledger.

12
00:00:58,242 --> 00:01:03,474
Evidence anchored on chain, and gasless releases signed once, off chain.

13
00:01:04,574 --> 00:01:09,230
Non-custodial by design, Bond never touches your funds.

14
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:15,626
Source verified on Sourcify, open source, with a half a percent fee frozen at creation.

15
00:01:15,806 --> 00:01:19,286
Not audited, and every page says so.

16
00:01:20,386 --> 00:01:25,690
Live now on Base Mainnet and Base Sepolia, with no accounts and no backend.

17
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:31,926
Bond, built for Base. Print your first escrow.
